WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.260
Data classification is foundational for LLM integrations.

2
00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:23.880
Prompts, files, retrieved passages, embeddings, model responses, tool results, logs, and conversation histories may contain personal data, customer data, secrets, source code, regulated information, contractual information, or sensitive business context.

3
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:29.420
These artifacts are often created automatically during normal use, which makes them easy to overlook.

4
00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:37.280
Treat them as data assets with owners, access rules, retention rules, and deletion paths.

5
00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:42.360
Context minimization means sending only the information needed for the approved task.

6
00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:50.220
A model does not need every document, every chat message, every profile attribute, or every database field to answer a focused question.

7
00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:59.840
Smaller, relevant context reduces privacy exposure, lowers cost, improves auditability, and can improve answer quality.

8
00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:07.060
The application should assemble context intentionally, using authorization filters and purpose limits rather than convenience dumps.

9
00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:13.100
Prompt retention, conversation storage, embeddings, and logs need clear rules.

10
00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:20.080
Storing prompts forever may preserve secrets, customer details, or source code long after the original task ended.

11
00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:25.940
Vector stores may retain sensitive material in forms that are not easily reviewed by humans.

12
00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:30.600
Conversation memory can unintentionally carry context from one task into another.

13
00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:37.580
Secure integrations define what is stored, why it is stored, who can access it, and when it is removed.

14
00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:42.100
Redaction and masking can reduce exposure, but they are not magic.

15
00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:50.520
Removing obvious secrets or personal identifiers is useful, yet the remaining context may still be sensitive or reidentifiable.

16
00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:55.100
The stronger control is to decide whether the model needs the data at all.

17
00:01:55.200 --> 00:02:05.920
Hosted versus local processing, provider boundaries, retention settings, and organizational policy should all be considered before sensitive data enters the LLM workflow.
